  "result": "Perfect! All 137 tests pass (121 original + 16 new). I've successfully added VAT functionality to the invoicing system.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **Created `lineVAT(line)`** function:\n   - Calculates VAT on the line amount AFTER discount is applied\n   - Formula: VAT = roundCents((lineTotal - lineDiscount) \u00d7 vatRate \u00f7 100)\n   - Clamped at 0 to never go negative\n\n2. **Updated `invoiceTotals(invoice)`** to return:\n   - `subtotal`: sum of all line totals\n   - `discount`: sum of all line discounts\n   - `vat`: sum of all line VATs (each calculated per line on amount after discount)\n   - `total`: subtotal - discount + vat (clamped at 0)\n\n3. **Updated `renderInvoiceText(invoice)`** to display:\n   - Line items as before\n   - Subtotal and Discount lines if discount > 0\n   - **VAT line if VAT > 0** (shown just above Total)\n   - Total line\n\n4. **Added 16 comprehensive tests** for VAT:\n   - Single line with different VAT rates (21%, 9%, 0%)\n   - VAT calculated on amount after discount\n   - Multiple lines with different VAT rates\n   - VAT with tier discounts\n   - Rendering with VAT display\n\n**Key behavior:**\n- VAT is always per-line, calculated on the amount **after** discount\n- VAT rates from catalogue: 21% (most items), 9% (print items), 0% (workshops)\n- No amount ever goes below zero (clamped at 0)\n- Invoice total = subtotal - discount + vat",
